.SH NAME
eventlog \- a logical object definition in the xCAT database.
.SH SYNOPSIS
.IX Header "SYNOPSIS"
\&\fBeventlog Attributes:\fR  \fIapplication\fR, \fIcomments\fR, \fIcomponent\fR, \fIdisable\fR, \fIeventtime\fR, \fIeventtype\fR, \fIid\fR, \fImessage\fR, \fImonitor\fR, \fImonnode\fR, \fInode\fR, \fIrawdata\fR, \fIrecid\fR, \fIseverity\fR
.SH DESCRIPTION
.IX Header "DESCRIPTION"
Logical objects of this type are stored in the xCAT database in one or more tables.  Use the following commands
to manipulate the objects: \fBmkdef\fR, \fBchdef\fR, \fBlsdef\fR, and \fBrmdef\fR.  These commands will take care of
knowing which tables the object attributes should be stored in.  The attribute list below shows, in
parentheses, what tables each attribute is stored in.
.SH "eventlog Attributes:"
.IX Header "eventlog Attributes:"
.IP "\fBapplication\fR (eventlog.application)" 6
.IX Item "application (eventlog.application)"
The application that reports the event.
.IP "\fBcomments\fR (eventlog.comments)" 6
.IX Item "comments (eventlog.comments)"
Any user-provided notes.
.IP "\fBcomponent\fR (eventlog.component)" 6
.IX Item "component (eventlog.component)"
The component where the event occurred.
.IP "\fBdisable\fR (eventlog.disable)" 6
.IX Item "disable (eventlog.disable)"
Do not use.  tabprune will not work if set to yes or 1
.IP "\fBeventtime\fR (eventlog.eventtime)" 6
.IX Item "eventtime (eventlog.eventtime)"
The timestamp for the event.
.IP "\fBeventtype\fR (eventlog.eventtype)" 6
.IX Item "eventtype (eventlog.eventtype)"
The type of the event.
.IP "\fBid\fR (eventlog.id)" 6
.IX Item "id (eventlog.id)"
The location or the resource name where the event occurred.
.IP "\fBmessage\fR (eventlog.message)" 6
.IX Item "message (eventlog.message)"
The full description of the event.
.IP "\fBmonitor\fR (eventlog.monitor)" 6
.IX Item "monitor (eventlog.monitor)"
The name of the monitor that monitors this event.
.IP "\fBmonnode\fR (eventlog.monnode)" 6
.IX Item "monnode (eventlog.monnode)"
The node that monitors this event.
.IP "\fBnode\fR (eventlog.node)" 6
.IX Item "node (eventlog.node)"
The node where the event occurred.
.IP "\fBrawdata\fR (eventlog.rawdata)" 6
.IX Item "rawdata (eventlog.rawdata)"
The data that associated with the event.
.IP "\fBrecid\fR (eventlog.recid)" 6
.IX Item "recid (eventlog.recid)"
The record id.
.IP "\fBseverity\fR (eventlog.severity)" 6
.IX Item "severity (eventlog.severity)"
The severity of the event. Valid values are: informational, warning, critical.
